    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d279">

                <pb facs="0317" n="313" sameAs="frus:frus1939v03/pg313"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94119/G09: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bullitt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-11-09T18:00:00+00:00">November 9, 1939—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 9—2:52 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2706. My No. 2534, October 25 [<hi rendition="#italic">20</hi>], 5 p.m. Li
                    Yu-ying called on me this morning and stated that he had just received a
                    personal message from Chiang Kai-shek informing him that there was absolutely no
                    truth in the report that Germany had made any attempt to bring about peace
                    between Japan and China.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bullitt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
